# Runspool is local-first and needs no secrets to run: the engine and the
# built-in steps never need network access or API keys.
#
# A plugin that does need a secret refers to it by NAME in its config (for
# example `appsecret: WECHAT_APPSECRET`) and asks Runspool's credentials service
# for the value when it needs it. The default service (`credentials-local`)
# looks the name up, in order, in:
#   1. the macOS keychain, only if configured (`keychain:`);
#   2. the process environment, unless configured off (`environment: false`);
#   3. $XDG_CONFIG_HOME/runspool/credentials.yaml (default
#      ~/.config/runspool/credentials.yaml), a `NAME: value` file;
#   4. a `.env` file next to the profile (the config file), unless
#      `profile_dotenv: false`;
#   5. ~/.env, unless `home_dotenv: false`.
# So copying this file to `.env` next to your config.yaml makes its values
# available to plugins by name. Runspool does not load it into the process
# environment: a step that reads os.environ directly does not see it. Keep it
# out of version control and readable only by you (chmod 600 .env); `runspool
# doctor` reports a source it cannot read, without its content.
# Details: docs/architecture.md, "Credentials".
#
# Example (fictitious; set only names a plugin you use asks for):
# MY_SERVICE_API_KEY=
